ld/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a814509c-4749-52dd-b5dc-eeb409609ce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333302" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue of the system's matrix $A$ is $v=[1,\\text{ }0]^{T}.$ The vector $w=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix} & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{{field-1}}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}{{field-2}},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on the \n{{field-3}} \nSince ${e}^{-t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/8d/8dc90697da27e52e0c1818d5529247d132944f30603936bedc191c4a14cb7d9c.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={{field-6}} \\\\ y &={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2.72$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $2.72$ | $1$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/1f/1f1d0d467285e26c4fc2f609c70d80fbb88867b77cdeb32c2a829006cbccea8e.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f7/f7413babbb41aff9a892593d73c257d01ff24f2441f169e6089773b23434a5ab.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-1,\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix} & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}t{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/8d/8dc90697da27e52e0c1818d5529247d132944f30603936bedc191c4a14cb7d9c.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t{e}^{-t} \\\\ y &={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2.72$ | $0$ | $0.30$ |\n| $y$ | $2.72$ | $1$ | $0.61$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/1f/1f1d0d467285e26c4fc2f609c70d80fbb88867b77cdeb32c2a829006cbccea8e.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f7/f7413babbb41aff9a892593d73c257d01ff24f2441f169e6089773b23434a5ab.png)"} :step/id #uuid "be046998-fcd4-5bf6-9080-bdee8bd453b5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478488}}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477732}]}
